  "EditorMetadata": {
    "Description": "P1b (Hill-attack -\u003E Blueprints migration, wave-core slice, architect Architect_Question_8_Wave_Core.md): Condition_IsWaveCompleted rebuilt as a visually-authored AiPrimitive BTreeAction (Intent=Action, not Condition -- both wave-core graphs return the full tri-state NodeStatus and a Condition\u0027s bool wrapper would collapse Running). WorkingState holds ONE bundled var, Wave:Hrot.AI.Behaviors.Brains.WaveState (Runners:MemberSlotList \u002B BurnedSlotsMask/BaselineReservedMask:UInt16), because the oracle\u0027s reverse-walk-with-swap-remove mutator has no visual-node form (architect Q#8-A). Graph: EventEntry -\u003E SetVariable(Wave) [Value \u003C- FunctionCall WaveMonitorOps.Update(s \u003C- GetVariable(Wave)) [IsPure, TrailingContext=View]] -\u003E Branch(Condition \u003C- Compare(FunctionCall WaveMonitorOps.ActiveCount(s \u003C- the SAME Update.Return), Literal Int32 0, Equal)) -\u003E True: Return(Success) (wave complete); False: Return(Running) (still polling). The single Update.Return output pin fans out to BOTH the SetVariable writeback AND the ActiveCount read (pure data nodes fan out freely, proven by HillAssault2_RequestAreaQuery), avoiding any re-read-before-write ordering hazard. New curated helper: Hrot.AI.Behaviors.Brains.WaveMonitorOps (Update/ActiveCount) -- the swap-remove reverse walk, BehaviorState-hash latch, and slot-mask release stay in a reviewable curated kernel; the visual graph is the thin Running/Success routing around it (architect Q#8-A/B). Does not modify the C# oracle (HillAttackCommanderNodes.Condition_IsWaveCompleted, line 447-503) or the compiler.",
    "Category": null,
